ure model would record."}},"significance":{"type":"score","instructions":"How architecturally significant is this symbol within its codebase?","criteria":["0: implementation detail (private helper, formatter, trivial wrapper, constant)","1: minor internal unit that only its file cares about","2: notable internal unit a maintainer would name when explaining the module","3: architecturally significant (a service, component, contract, store, policy or integration point)","4: core architectural element: an entry point, system boundary, or central abstraction"]},"concern_authentication":{"type":"noul","instructions":"This symbol itself implements the authentication concern (verifies identity: login, tokens, API keys, sessions, credentials), not merely calling something that does."},"concern_authorization":{"type":"noul","instructions":"This symbol itself implements the authorization concern (decides what an identity may do: roles, permissions, policies, access checks), not merely calling something that does."},"concern_data_persistence":{"type":"noul","instructions":"This symbol itself implements the data persistence concern (reads or writes durable storage: files, databases, caches, manifests on disk), not merely calling something that does."},"concern_external_integration":{"type":"noul","instructions":"This symbol itself implements the external integration concern (calls or serves an external system or process: HTTP clients, MCP servers, subprocesses, third-party APIs), not merely calling something that does."},"concern_observability":{"type":"noul","instructions":"This symbol itself implements the observability concern (telemetry, logging, metrics, tracing, spans), not merely calling something that does."},"concern_user_interface":{"type":"noul","instructions":"This symbol itself implements the user interface concern (renders or drives a user-facing interface: CLI output, web UI, TUI, prompts), not merely calling something that does."}}}

